n/build seon`, and so of the `:build` effect after merges) runs Tailwind's standalone binary, pinned by version and checksum and fetched once into `target/tailwind/`, into `target/css/app.css` (`:seon.config.web/stylesheet`, served at `/app.css` and read per request); its stamp is the digest of `input.css` and the scanned sources, so unchanged inputs regenerate nothing (68 ms when they changed, v1's port of its `bin/css`). Add a class to a render, or a token or safelist entry to `input.css`, and build: the stylesheet regenerates." "docs/render.md#the-page 23%: Every page is the render of a ctx through the one walk (```seon.render/walker```), laid out in root's chrome (```seon.render.ui/page-chrome```: the agents list, the head, the task's list, the conversation, the tiles), each placed component a unit whose input is its revision (owner, 2026-10-26: \"There is only one context rendering system and it needs to be built from the parts\"; 2026-10-25: the web UI finished from notes/design-agent-view-2026-10-24.md §5 and the mockup of 4624f2f4f, not redesigned)." "docs/render.md#the-models-context-a-cached-prefix-then-the-turn 18%: A model request sends what does not change first, so the provider serves it from its prefix cache, and sends nothing twice." "docs/failure-points.md#edges-that-catch-each-names-its-one-variant 17%: The failure points whose edge function catches, each with the one variant it declares and who handles it as data." "docs/forks.md#datahike 15%: `reference-code/datahike` pinned at `a9df162d`, the tip of ``jolt/own-suites-on-jolt`` (tests only: `a989ac4a` the core suites load on Jolt, `datahike.test.utils`, `api-test` and `core-test` requiring the hitchhiker tree and `kaocha.stacktrace` only on the JVM; `a9df162d` the tests our commits left stale: `query-cache-test` reads a failed call's message as the cause `6b668f0` wraps, `versioning-test` reads the roster through `branches` (`c0f9149`) and names a transaction id past every branch's (`be25be4`), `gc-test` counts the roster's two records, `query-ir-test` expects Jolt's per-cursor merge; [own suites](#own-suites)), on `e8a2999d`, the tip of ``jolt/attr-compare-mixed-kinds`` (`cmp-attr-nil` compares two attributes of one kind, keywords, entity ids or strings, with no `try`, and any other pair through `safe-compare`: a variable attribute bound to a string, long or symbol is a slice bound no stored attribute compares with, which since `cc614f4e` threw `ClassCastException` where it had joined nothing, and Seon's `[?f ?a ?s]` with `?a` an input in `seon.docs` reaches it."], :functions [["seon.render.proc/agent-view 10%: View's page when it names an agent (entity eid on main db): its components as its process drew them (ask-parts, seon.repl/render-ctx: the units of its walk), else, with no process to ask or none that answered, as root draws them from its branch (seon.ctx/build, drawn once by the same walk and layout: seon.render/draw) with main's renders, the page saying so." [:seon.agent/branch :seon.agent/description :seon.agent/id :seon.agent/key :seon.agent/opened :seon.agent/pid :seon.agent/status :seon.error/message :seon.eval/id :seon.eval/opened :seon.render/agent-input :seon.render/render-ctx :seon.run/agent :seon.run/task :seon.task/execution :seon.task/id]] "seon.root/observed-keys 7%: The members of an agent's view entry recorded on its entity (seon.task/agent-tx)." ["seon.turn/act! 7%: One model turn: the context of what was observed to the model, the reply's eval calls through the one REPL path, each answered as its own result, the turn's facts on the branch." [:seon.config.ai/cache-block-tokens :seon.run/id :seon.task/id :seon.turn/basis :seon.turn/calls :seon.turn/error :seon.turn/errors :seon.turn/finish :seon.turn/forms :seon.turn/id :seon.turn/model :seon.turn/ms :seon.turn/n :seon.turn/origin :seon.turn/reasoning :seon.turn/red :seon.turn/reply :seon.turn/run :seon.turn/sent :seon.turn/split :seon.turn/tokens :seon.turn/truncated]] ["seon.server/