{:task "seon.program/an-import-reads-each-form-once", :plan "Done (worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23, task seon.derive/one-content-keyed-derivation's cold paths). seon.source/import-tx of src and test (115 files, 2,409 forms) measured 541M ticks, 3,553 MB and 640k contracted calls cold, about 1.5 MB a form. Where it goes, by phase over the whole tree (warm): Jolt's analyzer 243M ticks and 1,150 MB (~2.6 KB an IR node, 442k nodes); unit-account 75M and 717 MB, of which seon.program/quoted-vars 28M and 492 MB over 140k constants (3.5 KB each: tree-seq, a set and its contract on every keyword and string); account 95M and 697 MB, with macro-uses reading the form's text a second time (27M, 119 MB) and tree-seq walking it (Jolt's tree-seq is ~1.1 KB a node visited); read-forms 34M and 141 MB; account-tx 28M and 148 MB; hasch form ids 17M and 142 MB. Fixed here, at their cause: a scalar constant that is no qualified symbol is not walked (unit-account), and account takes the form as read (:form, required by its contract; seon.source/accounts and seon.repl pass theirs), so macro-uses walks it and the text is read once. After: 497M ticks, 3,213 MB, 519k calls cold (-8%, -10%, -19%). Not fixed here, each its own task: Jolt's analyzer allocation per node (being measured); tree-seq's per-node cost (Jolt's clojure.core); 354 B per armed contracted call (seon.cost/units :fn/armed-call) on hot private helpers (vsym, datum, invoked: 5 calls per IR call node). Replaces the second read; deletes nothing.", :changed #{"seon.program/unit-account" "seon.repl/wrap-record" "seon.program/account" "seon.source/accounts" "seon.program/macro-uses"}, :shown {:sections ["docs/source.md#mains-program-follows-the-tree 56%: Main's program is the tree's: at each boot, when the files read differently from main's last import (their digest differs from the fact's `:digest`, or none is recorded), main's program is replaced by the tree's in one transaction, ```seon.source/replace-tx```; when they read the same, nothing is imported or written. So a resumed main follows its tree when worktree sessions merge and the tree moves on in git, or the next generation's tree holds Seon's own merges commit. Re-importing changed files alone would not do: a form's identity is its text (`seon.program/account-tx`), so a changed file's new forms would join its old ones, and a removed function would stay live. `replace-tx` is ```seon.source/import-tx```, read against main without the forms of the imported namespaces (each form takes its file's order and lead), with every program entity of those namespaces and of the schema resources that the import no longer makes retracted: a changed function's old form, a removed function's form and var, a removed file's namespace. Data (tasks, runs, turns, config and root facts) and the program of a namespace no file holds (an example program, a namespace an agent made) are untouched; history keeps the old program. A form or schema entry main holds already keeps its `:form/source` as it is, so a form merged in (which the binary does not hold) is still loaded at boot, and a form new to main is the binary's. The digest is of what was read (the files and the reference-code pins), not of the commit alone, so uncommitted edits in the tree count, and a merges commit made by `update-ref` under a checked-out tree (its files unchanged) imports nothing." "docs/source.md#tests-run-by-reach 42%: A test runs only when something it reaches changed since it was last green, in any checkout (task `seon.program/tests-run-by-reach`). ```seon.program/reach-digests``` gives each test of a db its reach digest: its own form, its namespace's forms that define no var (the ns form, fixtures), and every live form their `:form/refs` reach (a var to the form that last defined it; a defined multimethod's methods and protocol's extensions), and every schema entry a reached var's contract names (and each entry the entry's form names, on), each form and entry digested once; plus the checkout's inputs with no program facts (`seon.fx/inputs`: deps.edn, bin/, resources/ with the schemas contracts name, test fixtures and every submodule pin, Jolt's included; not task files or prose; and the per-test tick bound), plus the values of the config keys its reach reads (```seon.program/config-reads```: the `seon.config.*` keys its reached forms name, every key for one referencing the config map from outside `seon.config`, such as root's boot; their values from the config in force, ```seon.fx/config-input```: the shipped file, the `--config` layers the command line names, the `--set` overrides and the `#env` values under the profile, with the checkout's path normalized and the place keys left out), plus the vars data names that root resolves by name (`seon.fx/declared-refs`: system.edn's procs, edges of `seon.system/read-decl`), and no tree: a test whose reached forms call a file reader or run the binary (`seon.program/tree-readers`; a test runs target/seon, bin/root or bin/check only through `seon.test-store/binary-sh`) is digested by what it reaches like any other (owner, 2026-10-27: \"no tests should include all of src\"; with the tree it was 286 tests rerun on any edit), and a file or a binary change outside its reach is found by the full run (`bin/test --all`, below). A check step whose reach reads the tree still takes it. A test's digest moves exactly when a form or schema entry it reaches does. A literal name a form passes to `resolve`, `ns-resolve` or `requiring-resolve` is a reference (`seon.program/resolved`): the var it looks up at run time is one it reaches, so a test that resolves its var by name is no green reused after that var changes, or once it comes to exist. Any other name a form holds as data (quoted: `tree-readers`, `env-readers`, `seon.config/schema-forms`, whose `:seon.render/*` properties name every render, a form sent to an agent) is no reference, so reaching that form is neither using nor reaching what it names (below)." "docs/forks.md#jolt 17%: `reference-code/jolt` pinned at `6e604ac8`, the tip of ``jolt/emit-string-literals``, on `eba8826a`, the tip of ``jolt/image-fn-forms-opt-in``, on `2a6ae8f8`, the tip of ``jolt/arrays-compare``, on `86f49de8`, the tip of ``jolt/analysis-lookups``, on ``jolt/record-field-binds`` `0d39edc3`, on `e0351af8` (``jolt/global-ids-pin``: ``jolt/pin-2026-10-23`` `f05de7db` with ``jolt/hashset-bulk`` `ce384f07` merged in)." "docs/cost.md#how-we-measure 15%: Every measurement, in a cost proof or outside one, starts from a written estimate and is read across sizes, never from one quick run (owner: \"think about things algorithmically first and always put estimates on things\"):" "docs/cost.md#where-it-is-used 14%: An agent's task names its cost proofs as goals ([agent](agent.md)); `bin/test` runs them with every other test; a proof's `:ops` are priced in ticks, bytes and time from the unit table `seon.cost/units`, which `seon.cost-test/the-unit-table-is-current` measures again and holds to 1.25x."], :functions ["seon.program/account 5%: The program account of one top-level form, or nil when it is none of the program's." ["seon.source/text-tx 3%: The facts of text's forms as namespace nsym's program on db (seon.program/account-tx per form, in file order), with the namespace's file (relative path, or nil) and the text after its last form." [:form/source :ns/file :ns/name :ns/tail :seon.db/tx-data]] ["seon.root/import-source! 2%: Main's program follows Seon's own source (seon.source): root's dirs read through the :source effect (first brought to the main checkout's branch, seon.fx/read-source: fast-forwarded when behind, a recorded gap when it holds commits main lacks; their files, the tree's HEAD commit and its reference-code pins, and the tree's inputs with no program facts, seon.fx/inputs)." [:form/id :ns/file :schema/file :seon.error/message :seon.error/subject :seon.root/id :seon.root/source]] "seon.source/load-order 2%: The Clojure files ({relative path 